uh we got a call from a viewer last week  who brought up china  and a discussion of the portrayal of  china in american media  and during that conversation during that  phone call we talked about xenophobia  towards asian americans over covid we  talked about intellectual property theft  and a few other topics and i got a very  good email from thomas over the weekend  and thomas said to me you know david  um there is a china story to talk about  but it's not really what the caller  brought up intellectual property theft  it's an issue it's not the major  geopolitical issue with china  there's no real evidence that china  intentionally released covet as a bio  weapon so that's not really like the big  story with china yes xenophobia against  asian americans for real or perceived  misdeeds by china is something we should  be against we're not going to be  xenophobic against asian americans  because of something the chinese  government did that that's happening and  that's bad  but thomas wrote there are real issues  with the chinese communist party now  that's another issue to clarify  the ccp and china  as in chinese people are two different  things we're really talking about the  chinese government the chinese communist  party and as thomas wrote to me  there's a ton of negativity towards  china in general that's very surface  level some of it is based in plain old  bigotry some of it is peddled by u.s  media but there are many real reasons to  be at odds with the actions of the  chinese communist party so let's look at  the real concerns with the chinese  government the ccp  and these are not reasons to go to war  with china caveat i'm not suggesting war  i know that there's people possibly on  the revolutionary left who will see this  segment and say i'm calling for another  american military intervention no the  i'm not even saying these are reasons to  no longer trade with china if we stop  trading with china would be disastrous  for the american economy as it's  currently set up we're just going to  talk about issues with the chinese  government first  the ongoing uyghur genocide uyghurs are  a muslim ethnic minority in china china  has been credibly accused of committing  crimes against humanity possibly  genocide against the uyghur population  and other mostly muslim ethnic groups in  the northwest region of xinjiang  leading human rights groups including  amnesty and human rights watch have put  out reports accusing china  of crimes against humanity for their  actions there are re-education camps  there are horrifying things and much has  been written about it that's a real  substantive issue  with the chinese government second organ  harvesting this is all  the if you put a positive spin on it  this is oh  we get organ donations from prisoners  who have died of natural causes that's  the story that china would tell  but a tribunal ruled in 2020 that china  is forcibly harvesting organs from  prisoners prisoners who certainly didn't  volunteer to donate organs but it goes  even further possibly even prisoners who  are killed for organs not who have died  naturally  the number of transplant centers in  china has gone up over 300 percent wait  times for organs have come down  dramatically it's not clear why china  doesn't have much in terms of an  organized organ donation program how is  it happens how has it happened it seems  this is a likely explanation and it is  absolutely horrifying  note that back in 2012  a top chinese official said china is  going to phase out the practice of  taking organs from prisoners who have  been executed as of 2020 we believe that  that's still going on even if it's not  aside from executed there's a lot of  other ways that you can accelerate the  process of obtaining organs from  prisoners it seems that that's being  done absolutely horrifying number three  china so poorly mismanages its own  infrastructure  that it likely has led to hundreds or  more chinese people it's hard to get  real numbers from the ccp to die  due to flooding and the idea here is  that yes there have been heavy  rainstorms that are not man-made right  humans didn't make the rainstorms but  there are serious allegations that the  deaths are a result of this  infrastructure madness craze in china  where money is poured into projects that  look good  sometimes generate returns for people  but meanwhile simple infrastructure that  could be improved to prevent senseless  death from heavy rains and people  drowning are ignored okay complete  mismanagement that's a real criticism of  what's being done and then such  corruption from the ccp that causes all  sorts of problems massive fraud  embezzlement around these half-finished  villages where people make a ton of  money the projects are abandoned after  the contracts and the cash are handed  out as well as reconstruction projects  that never really happen although many  people get rich from them and then  lastly and this is a really big deal  a china's continued aggressive posturing  towards india taiwan and the south and  east china seas more generally each of  which we've talked about a little bit in  the past so on india there have been  somewhere between four and ten  skirmishes of note between india and  china over the border various face-offs  we've talked about it a little bit on  the bonus show before  the situation in the south china sea  involving china the philippines and  vietnam where you see military activity  by china naval maneuvers other  aggression outposts being built  concerning and then also conflicts with  japan and the east china sea um other  part of the sea it include uh it  includes japan having scrambled jets in  the past and other uh escalations so to  be clear again i want to be really  careful  i don't want war with china i'm not  saying invade china i'm not saying the  u.s doesn't also do bad things lots of  countries exhibit this type of  aggression  the difference is number one a lot of  the criticisms of china in the u.s media  and from you know people like trump have  been very surface level and lead to  xenophobia against asian americans which  has no place whatsoever there are actual  horrible things being done by the  chinese government many countries that  also want to do horrible things don't  have both the aggression and the the  means to carry it out the financial  resources at their disposal the massive  population that china has bigotry  against asian americans because of this  or chinese people anywhere is wrong and  we're against it  i'm also not saying cut off china from  an economic standpoint our economy is  now too inter intertwined with china's  it would take a really long time to be  able to unentangle that relationship  without destroying the american economy  so i'm not calling for that but there  are real geopolitical issues here and  humanitarian issues about which we  should be concerned it's not bigotry to  talk about that and the american media  rarely touches these actual issues  let me know what you think we'll have  more on this story on the david pakman  show instagram which you can find at  david pakman's show on instagram
 

